# BOOTARGS is baked into boot.scr at image build time (mkimage.sh) and is
# fixed for the whole rk3566 platform. It CANNOT read the per-device traits
# file (/mnt/sdcard/.minime/traits), which is generated at runtime by
# init.d/traits from /usr/share/minime/traits.
#
# fbcon=rotate:1 affects ONLY the kernel boot console (fbcon) — the transient
# text shown before the UI takes over. The UI (SDL/KMSDRM) is NOT affected:
# its orientation comes from the per-device `screen_rotation` trait
# (init.d/traits -> UI rotation). This value is
# therefore a boot-console-only quirk, intentionally NOT trait-derived, and it
# cannot be correct for every rk3566 device (ARC=90, RG353 family=270,
# RG503/RG DS=0).
BOOTARGS="fbcon=rotate:1 cma=256M"
DEFAULT_DEVICE="rk3566-anbernic-rg-arc-d.dtb"
EXTRA_ENV=""
